<%- include('../partials/head') %><%- include('../partials/nav', {active:'letters'}) %>
<%#
  Appointment letters.

  Shaped like Certificates -> Generate, on purpose: the list is the PEOPLE, and
  each row issues for that person. Starting from the person is the direction the
  work actually runs in — somebody has been hired, and the letter follows.

  The terms live in a <details> per row rather than on a separate page. A letter
  needs nine or ten fields, which is too many for an inline cell and not worth a
  page load, and keeping them attached to the row means you can never lose track
  of who you are writing to. Same pattern as the payment panel on the member
  list, so it is a form the office has already learned.

  PREVIEW BEFORE ISSUE. Preview renders the letter from whatever is typed, with
  a SPECIMEN watermark, and writes nothing. Issue mints the serial and saves the
  row. That order matters: a serial is permanent and appears on a document that
  leaves the building, so it should not be spent on a first draft.
%>
<style>
.ap-head{display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:flex-end;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:16px}
.ap-search{flex:1;min-width:220px;max-width:380px}
.ap-search label{margin-top:0}
.ap-panel{margin:0}
.ap-panel > summary{
  list-style:none;cursor:pointer;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;
  padding:8px 15px;border-radius:100px;background:var(--purple);color:#fff;
  font:500 .82rem 'Work Sans',sans-serif;white-space:nowrap}
.ap-panel > summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}
.ap-panel[open] > summary{background:var(--purple-deep)}
.ap-body{margin-top:10px;padding:16px 18px;border:1px solid var(--rule-strong);
  border-radius:var(--radius-sm);background:var(--paper-2);min-width:520px}
.ap-body .row{display:grid;gap:10px;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}
.ap-body .row3{display:grid;gap:10px;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr 1fr}
.ap-body label{margin-top:10px;font-size:.78rem}
.ap-body input,.ap-body select{padding:9px 11px;font-size:.85rem}
.ap-acts{display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:center;margin-top:14px;flex-wrap:wrap}
.ap-note{font-size:.75rem;color:var(--text-soft);margin:10px 0 0}
.ap-has{font-size:.74rem;color:var(--text-mute)}
.ap-ser{font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:.78rem;color:var(--purple);white-space:nowrap}
.ap-tbl th:nth-child(1){width:26%}
.ap-tbl th:last-child{width:22%}
@media(max-width:880px){
  .ap-body{min-width:0}
  .ap-body .row,.ap-body .row3{grid-template-columns:1fr}
}
</style>

<div class="wrap">
<p class="eyebrow">Documents</p>
<h1 style="margin-bottom:6px">Appointment letters</h1>

<% if (saved === 'withdrawn') { %>
  <div class="alert ok">Withdrawn. The reference now verifies as withdrawn rather than valid.</div>
<% } else if (saved === 'restored') { %>
  <div class="alert ok">Restored. The reference verifies as valid again.</div>
<% } else if (saved) { %>
  <div class="alert ok">
    Issued — reference <span class="serial"><%= saved %></span>. It is in the register below;
    open the PDF from there whenever you need a copy.
  </div>
<% } %>
<% if (error === 'member') { %><div class="alert err">Pick an active member. A letter prints and verifies against a Member ID, so it needs one.</div><% } %>
<% if (error === 'name') { %><div class="alert err">The letter needs a name to be addressed to.</div><% } %>
<% if (error === 'designation') { %><div class="alert err">The letter needs a designation — it is the subject line and the thing the letter proves.</div><% } %>

<p class="muted" style="max-width:80ch">
  The letter is generated when you ask for it, from the terms saved against it — nothing is
  stored as a file, so a reprint is always available and always matches what was issued.
  <strong>Preview</strong> shows the letter watermarked <em>specimen</em> without saving anything;
  <strong>Issue</strong> mints a permanent reference and records it.
</p>
<p class="muted" style="max-width:80ch">
  Only <strong>active members</strong> appear here. The letter carries a QR that verifies against
  the holder's Member ID, and a registration whose fee has not arrived does not have one yet.
</p>
<div class="alert err" style="max-width:80ch">
  <strong>Before the first real letter goes out:</strong> the general conditions printed on page 2
  — probation, confidentiality, safeguarding, notice, termination — are standard wording that has
  not been checked by a lawyer. Read them, and have whoever advises the trust read them. Everything
  else on the letter comes from the fields below; those seven clauses do not.
</div>

<div class="ap-head">
  <form method="get" action="/portal/admin/appointments" class="ap-search">
    <label for="q">Find an active member</label>
    <input id="q" name="q" value="<%= q %>" placeholder="Name, email or Member ID">
  </form>
  <div><a class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" href="/portal/admin/appointments">Clear</a></div>
</div>

<p class="muted" style="margin-top:-4px">
  <%= members.length %> active member<%= members.length === 1 ? '' : 's' %><%= q ? ' matching “' + q + '”' : '' %>.
</p>

<div class="card" style="padding:0;overflow-x:auto">
<table class="ap-tbl">
<tr><th>Member</th><th>Member ID</th><th>Letters</th><th>Issue a letter</th></tr>
<% if (!members.length) { %>
  <tr><td colspan="4" class="muted" style="padding:18px">
    <%= q ? 'Nobody matches that search.' : 'No active members yet — record a membership payment first.' %>
  </td></tr>
<% } %>
<% members.forEach(m => { %>
<tr>
  <td><b><a href="/portal/admin/members/<%= m.id %>"><%= m.name %></a></b><br>
      <span class="muted" style="font-size:.78rem"><%= m.email %></span></td>
  <td class="ap-ser"><%= m.memberId || '—' %></td>
  <td class="ap-has"><%= counts[m.id] ? counts[m.id] + ' issued' : '—' %></td>
  <td>
    <details class="ap-panel">
      <summary>Write letter</summary>
      <%#
        ONE form, TWO submit buttons with different formaction targets. Preview
        and Issue must send byte-identical fields — if they were two forms the
        two documents could differ, and a preview that does not match what gets
        issued is worse than no preview at all.
      %>
      <form method="post" action="/portal/admin/appointments?_csrf=<%= csrfToken %>">
        <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">
        <input type="hidden" name="userId" value="<%= m.id %>">
        <div class="ap-body">

          <div class="row3">
            <div>
              <label for="kind-<%= m.id %>" style="margin-top:0">Letter for</label>
              <select id="kind-<%= m.id %>" name="kind">
                <% kinds.forEach(k => { %><option value="<%= k %>"><%= kindLabel[k] %></option><% }) %>
              </select>
            </div>
            <div>
              <label for="ld-<%= m.id %>" style="margin-top:0">Letter date</label>
              <input id="ld-<%= m.id %>" type="date" name="letterDate">
            </div>
            <div>
              <label for="jd-<%= m.id %>" style="margin-top:0">Date of joining</label>
              <input id="jd-<%= m.id %>" type="date" name="joiningDate">
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="row">
            <div>
              <label for="desig-<%= m.id %>">Designation *</label>
              <input id="desig-<%= m.id %>" name="designation" required maxlength="120"
                     placeholder="Programme Coordinator">
            </div>
            <div>
              <label for="dept-<%= m.id %>">Department</label>
              <input id="dept-<%= m.id %>" name="department" maxlength="120"
                     placeholder="Community Development">
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="row">
            <div>
              <label for="rep-<%= m.id %>">Reporting to</label>
              <input id="rep-<%= m.id %>" name="reportsTo" maxlength="120" placeholder="Programme Manager">
            </div>
            <div>
              <label for="loc-<%= m.id %>">Place of posting</label>
              <input id="loc-<%= m.id %>" name="location" maxlength="120" placeholder="Bhadrak, Odisha">
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="row3">
            <div>
              <label for="et-<%= m.id %>">Employment type</label>
              <input id="et-<%= m.id %>" name="employmentType" maxlength="60" placeholder="Full time">
            </div>
            <div>
              <label for="prob-<%= m.id %>">Probation</label>
              <input id="prob-<%= m.id %>" name="probation" maxlength="60" placeholder="Six months">
            </div>
            <div>
              <label for="not-<%= m.id %>">Notice period</label>
              <input id="not-<%= m.id %>" name="notice" maxlength="60" placeholder="One month">
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="row3">
            <div>
              <label for="gm-<%= m.id %>">Gross per month (Rs.)</label>
              <input id="gm-<%= m.id %>" type="number" name="grossMonthly" min="1" step="1" placeholder="28000">
            </div>
            <div>
              <label for="ctc-<%= m.id %>">Annual, indicative (Rs.)</label>
              <input id="ctc-<%= m.id %>" type="number" name="annualCtc" min="1" step="1" placeholder="336000">
            </div>
            <div>
              <label for="hrs-<%= m.id %>">Working hours</label>
              <input id="hrs-<%= m.id %>" name="hours" maxlength="120" placeholder="09:30 to 18:00, Mon–Sat">
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="row">
            <div>
              <label for="addr-<%= m.id %>">Address on the letter</label>
              <input id="addr-<%= m.id %>" name="address" maxlength="240"
                     value="<%= m.city || '' %>" placeholder="Postal address">
            </div>
            <div>
              <label for="sig-<%= m.id %>">Signed by</label>
              <input id="sig-<%= m.id %>" name="signatoryName" maxlength="120" placeholder="Name of the signatory">
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <div>
              <label for="sigr-<%= m.id %>">Signatory's role</label>
              <input id="sigr-<%= m.id %>" name="signatoryRole" maxlength="120" placeholder="Secretary">
            </div>
            <div></div>
          </div>

          <p class="ap-note">
            Name, phone and email are taken from the member record. Blank fields print as a dash
            rather than a guess — a letter with an em dash on it is obviously unfinished, which is
            what you want.
          </p>

          <div class="ap-acts">
            <button class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" type="submit"
                    formaction="/portal/admin/appointments/preview?_csrf=<%= csrfToken %>"
                    formtarget="_blank">Preview (specimen)</button>
            <button class="btn btn-primary btn-sm" type="submit">Issue letter</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </form>
    </details>
  </td>
</tr>
<% }) %>
</table>
</div>
<% if (members.length >= 300) { %>
  <p class="muted" style="font-size:.8rem">Showing the first 300. Use the search to narrow it.</p>
<% } %>

<h2 style="margin-top:34px">Register of letters issued</h2>
<p class="muted" style="max-width:80ch">
  Every letter ever issued, whether or not it still stands. Withdrawing one does not remove it —
  the document is out there either way, and a scan has to be able to say "withdrawn" rather than
  "not recognised", which reads as forgery.
</p>

<div class="card" style="padding:0;overflow-x:auto">
<table>
<tr><th>Reference</th><th>Name</th><th>Designation</th><th>For</th><th>Dated</th><th>Status</th><th>Action</th></tr>
<% if (!letters.length) { %>
  <tr><td colspan="7" class="muted" style="padding:18px">No letters issued yet.</td></tr>
<% } %>
<% letters.forEach(l => { %>
<% var rev = revoked[l.serial]; %>
<tr>
  <td class="ap-ser"><%= l.serial %></td>
  <td><%= l.name %></td>
  <td><%= l.designation || '—' %></td>
  <td class="muted" style="font-size:.8rem"><%= kindLabel[l.kind] || l.kind %></td>
  <td class="muted" style="font-size:.8rem"><%= l.letterDate || '—' %></td>
  <td>
    <% if (rev) { %><span class="pill warn">Withdrawn</span>
    <% } else { %><span class="pill ok">Valid</span><% } %>
  </td>
  <td>
    <div class="mem-acts" style="display:flex;gap:5px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center">
      <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" href="/portal/admin/appointments/<%= l.id %>.pdf"
         target="_blank" rel="noopener">PDF</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" href="/verify/<%= l.serial %>"
         target="_blank" rel="noopener">Check a scan</a>
      <form method="post" style="display:inline"
            action="/portal/admin/appointments/<%= l.id %>/<%= rev ? 'restore' : 'revoke' %>"
            onsubmit="return confirm('<%= rev ? "Restore" : "Withdraw" %> <%= l.serial %>?')">
        <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">
        <button class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" type="submit"><%= rev ? 'Restore' : 'Withdraw' %></button>
      </form>
    </div>
  </td>
</tr>
<% }) %>
</table>
</div>
</div></body></html>
